ifest (frozen integrity check).\n\n12. report.md within 500 words.\n\nValidation plan (lightweight, independent):\n- Re-derive p-values for the top 2–3 terms with scipy's fisher_exact/hypergeom, and cross-check against gseapy's P-values. Also confirm the row count of res2d == 1818, and verify the BH-adjusted p-value for one term.\n- Confirm that the sha256 of the frozen files matches the input manifest.\n\nAlso, before running the full analysis, a quick check of counts ↔ layout mapping and DESeq2 runtime. 6 samples × ~20k genes — fast.\n\nPyDESeq2 0.5.0 details: DESeq class signature: DESeq(counts, metadata, design_factors, design=\"~condition\"?...). In 0.5.0: `DESeq(counts: pd.DataFrame, metadata: pd.DataFrame, design_factors: Union[str, List[str]], ..., ref_level: Optional[List[str]] = None, min_counts: int = 10, ...)`. Hmm — I need to verify the exact parameter names (0.5.0 is mid-2023?). Let me check the installed signature inside the venv.\n\nAlso, metadata index = sample IDs; counts columns = samples. PyDESeq2 requires counts as a DataFrame with genes as rows and samples as columns; metadata with samples as index.\n\nCooks filtering: default is refit_cooks=True, which is fine for n=3 vs 3.\n\nLet me quickly check pydeseq2's signature, then write analysis.py."}}
