ometric/Fisher one-sided, BH correction\"},\n  \"background_universe\": \"provided Reactome_2022.background.txt (used as the tested background)\",\n  \"policy\": \"no library download or substitution; per the input manifest's run_policy, used only the frozen inputs\",\n  \"environment\": {\"python\": ..., \"numpy\":..., \"pandas\":..., \"scipy\":...}\n}\n\nReport.md within 500 words.\n\nOK — writing the files. First, write analysis.py via Python heredoc through PowerShell's Set-Content? PowerShell here-strings do work: @'...'@ | Set-Content. Let me write it using that. Watch out for special characters — to be safe, write via a Python script (utf-8).\n"}}
